DEVIATIONS

This fork diverges from upstream Casdoor. Notable changes:

- Rebranded to "Hanzo IAM"; the Go module path is github.com/hanzoai/iam, and
  upstream "Casdoor" product naming is removed from product-facing surfaces
  (README, package.json, web UI titles).
- SuperAdmin / reserved `admin` org model: platform-wide privilege is membership
  in the reserved `admin` organization (User.IsSuperAdmin()), kept distinct from
  per-org admin. See object/organization_tenancy.go, object/check.go, and
  object/superadmin_test.go / object/security_test.go.
- White-label branding resolved by request domain (conf/brand.go,
  object/organization.go): one deployment serves hanzo.id and tenant white-label
  domains, each with its own branding and user pool.
- `<org>-<app>` application-naming convention enforced (object/application.go,
  validAppNamePattern).
- luxfi/* dependencies: github.com/luxfi/crypto, github.com/luxfi/kms (KMS-backed
  signing-key custody), and github.com/luxfi/metric.
- Capability-based authentication added (capauth package): typed, attenuable,
  revocable ZAP object-capability tokens replacing bearer-JWT on /v1/iam/whoami
  and follow-on endpoints.
- MCP and A2A identity surfaces added (mcp/, mcpself/) for AI-agent authentication.
- On-the-wire routes use the /v1/iam/* prefix (no /api/ prefix).
